// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 4-4, Revere Beach in the morning: sand, the boardwalk, the
// seawall, waves, sand sculptures, the old bandstand. Morning palette,
// bright and warm, same art language. Tiles are 16 x 16, anchor top left,
// variants with fps 0 (the rooftop layout). roofTop is dry sand (row 0 its
// sunlit crust, soft ripples; variant 1 footprints, variant 2 a scallop
// shell and weed) over compacted wet sand; roofEdgeLeft and roofEdgeRight
// slump to rounded shoulders; roofFill the wet sand's strata (variant 1 a
// buried clam shell and a pebble, variant 2 a crab's burrow); oneWay the
// silvered boardwalk on posts; stone a sunlit granite block of the
// seawall; spikes jagged rocks crusted with barnacles and mussel shells
// (hazard); brick a wooden lobster trap with its buoy (breakable); auraBlock
// the sigma crate in granite; vent a storm drain grate with a trickle; pipe
// a timber handrail run sideways (tileable).
//
// wave: 16 x 16, fps 8, loop, anchor bottom left (0, 16) on the sand's top.
// front (4 frames) is the leading edge rolling right (mirror for a wave
// rolling left): a thin sheet of water riding up, a curling foam lip
// churning. body (4 frames) is the water behind the front, tileable
// sideways, foam drifting. Draw body cells from x0 up to the front and the
// front cell at w.waves[i].front.
//
// sandSculpture: 32 x 24, anchor bottom left (0, 24), the breakable here (a
// big crab carved from packed sand on a plinth, the sculptor's bucket by
// it). idle 1 frame; crumble 3 frames played once (cracks, a slump with
// chunks breaking off, a low heap with grains flying), then draw nothing.
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left. Light sources, in decor pixels from the
// top left: boulevardLamp the globe at (8, 5) (faint in daylight).
// bandstand (the goal: the old cast iron bandstand, an octagonal pavilion
// with a flared green roof, a cupola and finial, cream columns, red railing,
// a raised granite floor with steps): 4 frames of the pennant on the
// finial waving, loop. Its roof is the high route's end; stand the goal on
// it.
//
// BEACH_GLOW lists the keys that glow: Y lamp globe, Z core, 0 warm, 1 sun
// glint, ^ ~ aura, 7 8 halos. Little light is needed in the morning.
//
// BEACH_BACKDROP: three 512 px tileable strips, bottom row one colour so it
// can be lifted. far (96): the ocean horizon, the morning sun with soft
// halo rings and a glitter path straight down the water (one sun per 512 px
// at the far layer's slow parallax), the headland curling at the left with
// a lighthouse, two small sails. mid (80): the far arm of the crescent
// across the bay: the boulevard's buildings small with distance, the old
// station's tower, trees, the lamp line, the seawall with its little green
// roofed pavilions, the bright beach, the bay's blue water in front. near
// (64): a low dune with beach grass leaning in the wind and a slatted snow
// fence, sand to the bottom.
